      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "These phrases are indeed common fillers known in rhetorical studies as \"bridge套\" or rhetorical bridges, used to smoothly transition between ideas without offering substantive content. While your observation about their frequency during major announcements is accurate, sociolinguistics suggests they primarily serve a pragmatic function of pacing rather than a structural mechanism designed to inherently shut down critical thinking. They often provide listeners a sense of procedural certainty during complex information processing, which can be misinterpreted as an intent to guide opinion rather than a neutral delivery tool.",
      "source": "target",
